+
+
+## Ascendant — Prismatic Dawn, milestone A
+
+The owner-supplied specification was moved intact into `alpha-updates/1.13.0-ascendant-cutscene/SPEC.md`. Only A is active. The descriptor contains prelude 1000, spark 3000, cave 4000, tip 1200, fall 800, impact 600, underwater 1900 and tendrils 2500 ms. These cover S0–S3's prescribed 0–15 s clock. A temporarily fades the pool into the quiet Ascendant field and performs the existing 400 ms flip; this is not the specified final S7/S8 ending.
+
+`crystal-scene-engine.js` extracts Mythical's native WebGL helpers, reflection targets, post-processing and disposal. `mythical-scene.js` is a compatibility facade. `cutscene-clock.js` extracts the existing clock for B to restyle. `cutscene-runtime.js` owns registered presentation factories, descriptor sections, beat emission, dev seeking/rate overrides, common two-second skip hint and 500 ms skip advancement. Existing opening updates still supply the only clock. Hidden time is excluded by the existing visibility handler. Ascendant warms programs, procedural geometry and targets during committed foil cutting. The scene uses serial-seeded hexagonal clusters, pastel dispersive refraction, procedural caustics, half-resolution reflection/bloom, an encoded 256/128 ping-pong height field on High/Medium and 20/10 rooted 28-segment Verlet ribbons; Low has analytic water and six sine ribbons. The live frame average can reduce one tier during S1/S2 and ramps resolution without changing descriptor durations. The visible canvas retains quality scaling and DPR cap 2. WebGL failure/context loss follows the Canvas narrative at the current section.
+
+`ascendant-background.js` exposes one seeded procedural white/pastel side/splash field. The Ascendant finish exposes `drawBackground` and samples the retained field's time while the reveal is active. Recovery restores the quiet field without initializing/replaying 3D. The complete S7/S8 continuous background clock, squircle draw, Short/Off choices and prescribed three-second light alternative remain C. Existing reduced/static alternatives remain operational for A; they are not the final light version.
+
+The dev registry adds Play Ascendant (sandbox), scrub, section jump, 0.1–4× timescale, renderer quality override, Mono and shared Skip. A's skip targets its completed ending; once C supplies the explosion section, the same skip mechanism targets that section and its single flash. Short/Full and the safe-flash graph remain C.
+
+Verification was restricted to one headed game launch and one dev-triggered Normal playthrough. It reached the revealed Ascendant card through all eight sections with WebGL2 and no console errors or warnings. No old tests, new tests, screenshots or profiling were run. No frame-rate, narrow-screen, context-loss, reload, skip or quality-matrix acceptance is claimed from that playthrough.
